 can't run VoiceOver/NVDA in this sandbox, so I audited the lightbox against how those readers behave and fixed the remaining issues: the live region now lives outside the dialog (so announcements fire reliably instead of at mount), the dialog uses a proper localized aria-label instead of pointing at the caption, all icon buttons and help text are translated per language, the lightbox image no longer double-announces its caption (alt="" with the visible figcaption), and the filter chips expose aria-pressed and reset the open image when the set changes.
